    "https://vsc.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Castleton-VT/Assistant-Professor-of-Business_R-2026336": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Business",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nVermont State University seeks applicaitons for a full-time, tenure track Assistant Professor position in the School of Business and Professional Studies. This position will be based on the Castleton campus. The new faculty member will be expected to teach a variety of business courses, including but not limited to Management, Marketing and Finance. In addition to teaching, faculty at VTSU are expected to participate in and contribute to university committees, scholarship and professional development, student advising, service to the university community, development of curriculum, and educational facilities as needed, and other duties related to teaching effectiveness, scholarship and service to the university. The successful candidate will have earned an MBA or related field, combiined with at least three years of significant experience and should have previous teaching experience at the undergraduate level. Candidates wit experience teaching in a variety of modalities (in-person, face-to-face-plus, asynchronous online) are encouraged to apply. Scheduled Hours Weekly: 37.5 Budgeted Wage for this Position: $57,500-$61,500 Exempt Status: Exempt Grade: F01 Job Posting Responsibilities: Unit Determination: Full-Time Faculty -VSC Faculty Federation"
    },
    "https://vsc.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Williston-VT/Assistant-Professor_R-2026382": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nVermont State University (VTSU), Williston/St. Albans campus invites applicants for a full-time faculty position in the Department of Nursing for the academic year 2026-2027, teaching across the Practical Nursing (PN) Program and Associate Degree in Nursing (ASN) Program. Qualified candidates will be offered a tenure-track position or a one-year terminal contract, renewable for three years, based on the individual's years of full-time clinical nursing experience and years of full-time teaching in an accredited nursing program. Each faculty member in the Department of Nursing is responsible for: 1. Contributing to the professional learning environment in the classroom and in clinical rotations. 2. Encouraging student learning and retention, consistent with the student learning outcomes and course objectives, nurturing an environment focused on providing the highest quality of care to patients. 3. Evaluating student acquisition of nursing competence. 4. Participating in the implementation, evaluation, and revision of the nursing curriculum and relevant policies. 5. Serving as an academic adviser to students across the programs. 6. Participating in assigned roles in the Department of Nursing standing committees. 7. Demonstrating continued professional development in the areas of nursing and nursing education commensurate with assigned roles. 8. Collaborating with healthcare partners across the state of Vermont. 9. Complying with the policies outlined by the Vermont State College system, Vermont State University, and the Department of Nursing. Specific Criteria for this position include: 1. An unencumbered Registered Nurse license allowing practice in Vermont. 2. Masters of Science in Nursing 3. A minimum of two years full-time, or the equivalent of, acute care nursing experience. 4. Commitment to the mission and vision of Vermont State University and the Department of Nursing. 5. Commitment to the integration of technology, including simulation across the curriculum. 6. Knowledge of processes related to NLN-CNEA Accreditation. 7. Occasional travel to other campus sites and/or clinical agencies in the region. Salary:  Based on qualifications and experience as defined by the VSC-VSCFF Bargaining Unit Agreement   Application Information:  Applicants interested in applying  must submit a Cover Letter, Resume/CV, and Unofficial College Transcripts (official transcripts will be required if hired).  Applications will be accepted until position is filled or by date specified. However, applications received after the initial screening will be considered at the discretion of Vermont State University. VTSU strongly encourages applications from members of ethnic minority groups and other under-represented backgrounds. VTSU is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate against any individual because of race, color, religion, ancestry, place of birth, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, national origin, age or veteran status, or against a qualified individual with a disability, or any other person whose status is protected under local, state or federal laws. In compliance with ADA requirements, we will make reasonable accommodations for the known disability of an otherwise qualified applicant. For more information visit the VSC system website www.vsc.edu/agreements-personnel-handbook/ All full-time and some part-time positions are subject to a criminal background check. Any offer of employment is conditional upon successful completion of these checks.   Scheduled Hours Weekly: 37.5 Budgeted Wage for this Position: $57,500 based on qualifications and experience as defined by the VSC-VSCFF Bargaining Unit Agreement. Exempt Status: Exempt Grade: F01 Job Posting Responsibilities: Unit Determination: Full-Time Faculty -VSC Faculty Federation"
    },
    "https://vsc.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Williston-VT/VTSU-Part-Time-Faculty-EMS-2010L_R-2026357": {
      "title": "VTSU Part-Time Faculty EMS-2010L",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nVermont State University School of Nursing & Health Sciences Invites applications for a Part-Time teaching position for Fall 2026 (August 24 - December 18, 2026) for EMS-2010 Lab - Principles & Practices of Paramedicine I Lab This position is for approximately 53 hour s for the semester. 2.36 teaching workload credits per semester. This course prepares the EMT or AEMT for a successful transition to paramedic-level practice through a flipped-classroom model with intensive laboratory days each week. Emergency Medical Technician level skills are verified, and the student is expected to expand upon prior knowledge to develop paramedic-level knowledge of foundational concepts, anatomy, physiology, and pathophysiology, assessment of ill and injured people across the lifespan, medication administration, and pharmacology. The student will advance their knowledge and skills related to the assessment and interdisciplinary management of conditions related to airway management, respiratory problems, and trauma. Clinical and field experiences in the first semester focus on developing these foundational skills and learning about the role of the paramedic. Minimum Qualifications : Bachelor's degree preferred and/or 2 to 4 years of experience in the paramedic field or a combination of education and experience from which comparable knowledge and skills are acquired. A Vermont Paramedic License or Vermont Registered Nurse License with EMS experience is required. Knowledge of course content being delivered. Excellent verbal, interpersonal, and written communication skills. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and flexible decision-making capabilities. AHA instructor status required for ACLS and PALS courses. Team Player with the ability to multitask in a fast-paced work environment. Ability to work under strict deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Ability to work with all levels of students as well as internal faculty and staff. Ability to endure considerable walking, standing, and lifting while instructing/supervising students. Ability to deal effectively with and represent the College to a broad range of individuals and groups within and outside of the College. All required immunizations must be up to date. Valid Vemront driver's license. Scheduled Hours Weekly: 3.53 Budgeted Wage for this Position: $1648.00 per teaching workload credit per the VSC Part-time faculty agreement Exempt Status: Exempt Grade: P01 Job Posting Responsibilities: Unit Determination: Part-Time Faculty - VSC Faculty Federation"
    },
    "https://vsc.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Castleton-VT/Graduate-Assistant-Coach--Women-s-Hockey-_R-2026375": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant Coach (Women's Hockey)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nVermont State University is seeking qualified candidates for Graduate Assistant Coach positions in Athletics. Graduate Assistant Coaches play an important role in supporting the success, development, and experience of our student athletes both on and off the field. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Assisting with the coordination and supervision of practices and contests;   Supporting recruitment activities for prospective student athletes; Coordinating team travel and meals; Assisting with eligibility procedures and compliance requirements; Supporting athletic communications and sports information functions; Performing additional duties as assigned. Graduate Assistant Coaches will report directly to the Head Coach of the assigned sport. Graduate Assistant Coach appointments are typically structured as two one-year appointments, contingent upon satisfactory academic progress, job performance, program needs, and approval by the University. Graduate Assistant coach positions include tuition remission for up to 18 graduate credits; on-campus housing and a $5,000 stipend. Under current IRS regulations, graduate tuition benefits exceeding the annual non-taxable threshold of $5,250 will be treated as taxable income and subject to applicable withholding taxes. Any resulting tax liability is the responsibility of the graduate assistant. Graduate Assistants are expected to maintain a minimum cumulative GPA of 3.0 and as representatives of Vermont State University, are expected to demonstrate professionalism, integrity, and good sportsmanship, while fostering those same expectations among student athletes. Adherence to all NCAA, conference, and university regulations is required. Appointment to a Graduate Assistant Coach position may be terminated in cases involving deliberate or serious violations of NCAA regulations or university policies. Scheduled Hours Weekly: 20 Budgeted Wage for this Position: $5,000 Exempt Status: Exempt Grade: STS Job Posting Responsibilities:"
    },
    "https://vsc.wd108.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Williston-VT/Professional-Pilot-Program-Instructor_R-2026279": {
      "title": "Professional Pilot Program Instructor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-08\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPart Time Instructor for Professional Pilot Program AER-2330: Aeronautical Physiology and Psychology M 2:00 PM - 4:50 PM 8/24/2026 - 12/18/2026 VTSU Williston Campus, Blair Park 202 (Lecture) Dates 8/24/2026 - 12/18/2026 Credits 3 Requisites None Course Description Pilots have unique mental and physical demands that are critical for their safety-sensitive roles in ensuring safety and passenger comfort. This course focuses on understanding these demands and ensuring compliance from a regulatory and an ethical standpoint. The physiology component focuses on general health with emphasis on altitude physiology, vision, hearing, medications, and fitness. The psychological component emphasizes aeronautical decision-making, risk management, sleep, and fatigue. Both are integrated into a discussion of the FAA medical certification process and pilot duties and responsibilities of compliance. Relevant experience should include Flight Instruction or Ground School Instruction of FAA License or Certification courses. Method:  This course is currently being taught on Mondays from 2:00PM to 4:50PM as an on-ground course at the Williston Campus. has context menu Scheduled Hours Weekly: 3 Budgeted Wage for this Position: $4944.00-$5358.00 Exempt Status: Exempt Grade: P01 Job Posting Responsibilities: Unit Determination: Part-Time Faculty - VSC Faculty Federation"
    },
