sive environment. Ability to work effectively with a wide range of individuals within the University and capacity to work as part of a team to collaborate and choose student success. Ability to collaborate effectively with college personnel as well as families/guardians and external resources in carrying out the various coordination, liaison, and advocacy aspects of the job. Ability to work some weekends and evenings to provide student support outside of normal business hours. Scheduled Hours Weekly: 37.5 Budgeted Wage for this Position: $44,000-45,000 Exempt Status: Exempt Grade: S12 Job Posting Responsibilities: Unit Determination: Professional, Administrative, Technical - VSC United Professionals"
